# Copy to ".env.development.local" (git-ignored) for local development.
# Use that name, NOT ".env.local": Expo loads ".env.local" in every mode,
# including when `eas update` bundles a test/production update on this PC,
# which would ship your local address to every installed phone.
# ".env.development.local" is only loaded by `npx expo start`.
#
# Which app to build: "test" (default) or "production".
# APP_VARIANT=test
#
# Backend address. Leave unset to use the variant's website
# (https://test.rwcrew.eu or https://rwcrew.eu). To develop against the
# backend running on your PC, use your PC's LAN IP (NOT localhost - on a phone
# that means the phone itself), with the phone on the same Wi-Fi:
# API_URL=http://192.168.1.50:8020
